{
	"about": "keptQuery(search) as packages/api/src/v1/query.ts computes it (DEC-023): what is kept of a screenshot's query. An implementation in another codebase has to give out for every in, and hold the same words and names. The rule: the leading ?s are taken off; split on &, an empty piece is dropped; a piece is a name and, after its first =, a value (none without =); a piece with a raw # is dropped; name and value are percent-decoded with + as a space, and a malformed escape (decodeURIComponent throws) drops the piece. The name's words: split before an upper-case letter that follows a lower-case letter or a digit, and between an upper-case run and an upper-case letter followed by a lower-case one, then at every character that is not an ASCII letter or digit, lowercased; the piece is dropped when a word is in words or the words joined are in names. The decoded name and the decoded value are each dropped when they contain @, match the JWT pattern eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]*\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]*\\. anywhere, or are 40 or more characters of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ - . ~ + / = only. Kept pieces keep their bytes and order, joined by &. When the result is longer than 1024 code points it is dropped whole: the output is empty. Never throws.",
